    "final_answer": "I have successfully filtered to Bachelor's degree programmes and found the following programs. Here are 3 Bachelor's degree programmes available on Coursera:\n\n## 3 Bachelor's Degree Programs on Coursera\n\n1. **Bachelor of Arts in Liberal Studies** - Offered by **Georgetown University**\n   - A liberal arts program that integrates business, technology, and global perspectives through interdisciplinary approaches. Up to 64 college credits can be transferred.\n   - Application deadline: October 14, 2026\n\n2. **Bachelor of Information Technology** - Offered by **Illinois Tech**\n   - Provides a comprehensive education in market-demanded cloud computing and security skills. No degree required; accepts applications through performance-based admission.\n   - Application deadline: October 19, 2026\n\n3. **Bachelor of Science in General Business** - Offered by **University of North Texas**\n   - Develops CORE skills in finance, marketing, and management at a top-ranked, AACSB-accredited institution, preparing students for various business roles.\n   - Application deadline: November 30, 2026\n\n### Additional Bachelor's Program Found:\n4. **Bachelor of Science in Computer Science** - Offered by **University of London**\n   - Builds a foundation in core mathematics, data, and programming skills for tech careers, with specializations in machine learning, AI, or UX.\n   - Application deadline: March 16, 2027\n\n**Note:** There are 11 Bachelor's degree programmes total on Coursera (after applying the Bachelor's degree filter). I successfully navigated to the online degrees section by clicking \"学位\" (Degrees) in the main navigation, then filtered by \"学士学位\" (Bachelor's Degree) to display only Bachelor's level programmes.",
